      <t:profileDesc xmlns:t="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
         <t:abstract>
            <t:ab>The Gadla Mātyās containing the Life, the Miracles and the Image of the saint, was probably composed 
               <t:date notBefore="1580" notAfter="1640" cert="medium">between the end of the 16th and the beginning of the 17th century</t:date>. 
               The only accessible witness is <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ANLcr84#p2">Rome, Biblioteca dell’Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei, Conti Rossini 84: msPart p2</t:ref>, which is a 20th-century copy from a manuscript, 
               which was kept at the church of Šǝmāgǝlle in <t:placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC3764Hamase">Ḥamāsen</t:placeName>.</t:ab>
         </t:abstract>
         <t:langUsage><t:language ident="en">English</t:language><t:language ident="gez">Gǝʿǝz</t:language></t:langUsage>
